   "gap": "Durrett PTE author version 5 of 11 January 2019, Theorem 1.6.2 (pp. 29-30, PDF pp. 37-38), accompanies Jensen's inequality with a worked two-point illustration (P(X = x) = t and P(X = y) = 1 - t give E phi(X) = t phi(x) + (1 - t) phi(y) >= phi(EX), i.e. the convexity inequality) and Figure 1.6 (phi(x) = x^2 - 3x + 3 with P(X = 1) = P(X = 3) = 1/2), and names the special cases |EX| <= E|X| and (EX)^2 <= E(X^2). The handbook theorem (integration-expectation.tex lines 292-301) has no worked example and no worked boundary of its probability-normalisation and integrability hypotheses; the two-point illustration and the Figure 1.6 example are not supplied anywhere on the route (the two special cases appear only separately, as the absolute-value bound and the variance identity).",
